<div class="bhd-page__keypoints" aria-label="Research partnership principles">
  <div><strong>Clear roles</strong><span>Researcher, advisor, investigator and company collaborator are distinct roles.</span></div>
  <div><strong>Evidence first</strong><span>Methods and claims should match the question being studied.</span></div>
  <div><strong>No borrowed endorsement</strong><span>An individual's institutional affiliation does not imply institutional endorsement of Best Hydrate.</span></div>
</div>

<section class="bhd-page__prose-grid">
  <article class="bhd-page__prose">
    <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Current collaboration</p>
    <h2>Dr. Spencer Proctor</h2>
    <p>Dr. Proctor is Professor and Department Chair in Agricultural, Food and Nutritional Science at the University of Alberta and Director of the Metabolic and Cardiovascular Diseases Laboratory. He is also Chief Scientific Officer of Best Hydrate and a co-author of our accepted Frontiers hydration review.</p>
    <p>His academic affiliation provides relevant scientific expertise. It does not mean the University of Alberta endorses Best Hydrate or its product claims.</p>
    <a class="bhd-page__text-link" href="https://apps.ualberta.ca/directory/person/proctor" target="_blank" rel="noopener">University of Alberta profile →</a>
  </article>
  <aside class="bhd-page__callout">
    <span class="bhd-page__callout-label">Research standard</span>
    <h3>Define the question before the result.</h3>
    <p>Roles, methods, data ownership and reporting expectations should be clear before a study begins.</p>
  </aside>
</section>

